Frozen v0.128.0 saves for the event-referent identity fix (CR 400.7): a triggered ability whose
"destroy that creature" names the damage recipient, saved with the trigger on the stack before
the event-referent identity pins existed. They exercise the restore path for released saves.

Generated by the RELEASED engine. Never regenerate with a newer engine: their value is
that they are byte-for-byte what v0.128.0 wrote.

Generating tag and commit: v0.128.0, 118107f087324479a6cff95a4f5cd1c68d99d32e
  (upstream phase-rs/phase).

Each board is built with GameScenario from verbatim Oracle text, parsed by the v0.128.0
parser, and driven by GameActions. None is recorded from play.

Serializer: engine-wasm export_game_state_json() (TrustedGameStateEnvelope::capture), compact
JSON, after installing the state in GAME_STATE; each file is then gzip-compressed at level 9
with no name and mtime 0 (equivalent to gzip -9n).

Command (in a worktree checked out at the commit above, with the generator below appended
to crates/engine-wasm/src/lib.rs):

  FIXTURE_DIR=<dir> cargo test -p engine-wasm --lib generate_v128_fixtures -- --nocapture
  gzip -9n <dir>/*.json

Fixtures (P0's precombat main; Dinosaur Hunter's trigger on the stack after Ram Through, Priority):
  hunter_trigger_pending: no response.
  hunter_trigger_pending_after_blink: P1's Ephemerate blinked the Dreadmaw (a new object, CR 400.7).

Generator source:

// Scratch generator for cluster-event-referent-identity's frozen v0.128.0 fixtures. Not for commit.
#[cfg(test)]
mod zz_v128_fixture_gen {
    use super::*;
    use engine::game::scenario::{GameRunner, GameScenario, P0, P1};
    use engine::types::actions::GameAction;
    use engine::types::game_state::{StackEntryKind, WaitingFor};
    use engine::types::mana::{ManaType, ManaUnit};
    use engine::types::phase::Phase;
    use engine::types::zones::Zone;

    const HUNTER: &str = "Whenever this creature deals damage to a Dinosaur, destroy that creature.";
    const RAM_THROUGH: &str = "Target creature you control deals damage equal to its power to \
target creature you don't control. If the creature you control has trample, excess damage is \
dealt to that creature's controller instead.";
    const EPHEMERATE: &str = "Exile target creature you control, then return it to the \
battlefield under its owner's control.\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile \
it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile \
without paying its mana cost.)";

    fn write(name: &str, state: GameState) {
        clear_game_state();
        let summary = format!(
            "wf={:?} stack={}",
            std::mem::discriminant(&state.waiting_for),
            state.stack.len()
        );
        GAME_STATE.with(|cell| cell.set(Some(state)));
        let json = export_game_state_json().unwrap();
        let dir = std::env::var("FIXTURE_DIR").expect("FIXTURE_DIR");
        std::fs::write(format!("{dir}/{name}.json"), &json).unwrap();
        println!("V128FIX {name} bytes={} {summary}", json.len());
    }

    fn pay(r: &mut GameRunner, player: engine::types::player::PlayerId, kinds: &[ManaType]) {
        for kind in kinds {
            r.state_mut()
                .add_mana_to_pool(player, ManaUnit::new(*kind, ObjectId(9_900), false, vec![]));
        }
    }

    fn hunter_on_stack(r: &GameRunner, hunter: ObjectId) -> bool {
        r.state().stack.iter().any(|e| {
            matches!(&e.kind, StackEntryKind::TriggeredAbility { source_id, .. } if *source_id == hunter)
        })
    }

    fn pass_until(r: &mut GameRunner, stop: impl Fn(&GameRunner) -> bool) {
        for _ in 0..100 {
            if stop(r) {
                return;
            }
            r.act(GameAction::PassPriority).expect("pass");
        }
        panic!("never reached");
    }

    fn board(blink: bool) -> GameRunner {
        let mut s = GameScenario::new();
        s.at_phase(Phase::PreCombatMain);
        let hunter = s.add_creature_from_oracle(P0, "Dinosaur Hunter", 2, 3, HUNTER).id();
        let dino = s
            .add_creature(P1, "Colossal Dreadmaw", 6, 6)
            .with_subtypes(vec!["Dinosaur"])
            .id();
        let ram = s.add_spell_to_hand_from_oracle(P0, "Ram Through", false, RAM_THROUGH).id();
        let eph = s.add_spell_to_hand_from_oracle(P1, "Ephemerate", true, EPHEMERATE).id();
        let mut r = s.build();
        pay(&mut r, P0, &[ManaType::Green, ManaType::Colorless]);
        r.cast(ram).target_objects(&[hunter, dino]).commit();
        pass_until(&mut r, |r| {
            hunter_on_stack(r, hunter)
                && r.state().objects[&ram].zone != Zone::Stack
                && matches!(r.state().waiting_for, WaitingFor::Priority { player } if player == P1)
        });
        if blink {
            let before = r.state().objects[&dino].incarnation;
            pay(&mut r, P1, &[ManaType::White]);
            r.cast(eph).target_object(dino).commit();
            pass_until(&mut r, |r| {
                r.state().objects[&eph].zone != Zone::Stack
                    && matches!(r.state().waiting_for, WaitingFor::Priority { .. })
            });
            assert_ne!(r.state().objects[&dino].incarnation, before, "blinked");
        }
        assert!(hunter_on_stack(&r, hunter), "Hunter trigger pending");
        r
    }

    #[test]
    fn generate_v128_fixtures() {
        write("hunter_trigger_pending", board(false).state().clone());
        write("hunter_trigger_pending_after_blink", board(true).state().clone());
    }
}
